WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.401
-Hello, everyone!
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.869
to "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:07.306
[ Cheering and applause ]
here in Studio 6A!

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.676
[ Laughs ]
You having a little trouble?

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.710
-Got caught.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.878
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:15.215
-I was watching you try to play
drums -- taking it off.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:18.718
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.119
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.622
Well, guys, with Election Day
less than a week away,

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.624
the White House Science Office
just put out an interesting list

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:28.394
of President Trump's
accomplishments.
Listen to this.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.229 line:0%
-The White House
Science Policy Office

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:34.133 line:0%
lists ending the pandemic
as one of what it calls

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.036 line:0%
the top accomplishments of the
president's first term.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.805
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.273
-What?!

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.908
That's like the Tampa Bay Rays

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.008
listing their biggest
accomplishment

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:45.110
as 2020 World Series champions.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.315
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.250
Seriously, right now,
the coronavirus is like,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.786
"Ending the pandemic?

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.020
Thanks to you,
we just got picked up

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.020
for three more seasons."

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.890
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.693
Keep in mind, though,
the White House "Science Office"

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.663
is just Eric and Don Jr. wearing
a Bill Nye Halloween costume.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.565
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.566
When I think of the
White House Science Office,

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.368
I picture a bunch of monkeys
in lab coats

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.236
running around with their
fingers stuck in test tubes,

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:12.472
like throwing papers.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.039
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:16.175
I was pretty surprised to find
out the Trump White House

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:17.877
has a Science Office.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.244
It's like finding out
"The Bachelorette"

00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:20.546
has a Science Office.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:26.552
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.721
To be fair, lying on his résumé

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.057
is one of the most relatable
things Trump's ever done.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.992
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.527
I don't know how to use Excel.

00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:37.230
Trump ended the pandemic.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.297
Now, everyone is just living

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.699
in their parents'
basement for fun.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.433
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:42.602
What an incredible claim.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.771
Someone hasn't been
that far off since...

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:51.544 line:0%
-Fred Flintstone!

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.678 line:0%
-No.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:56.182
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.351
-I knew it.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.854
I knew it.
I knew it. I knew it.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:02.288
[ Laughter and applause
continues ]

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.491
Oh, now y'all here
and y'all laughing.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.192
[ Laughter and applause
continues ]

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.660
Word? Okay.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:13.866
[ Laughter and applause
continues ]

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.702
-Whoo!
-Oh, my God.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:18.504
That was close.
Close.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:21.240
[ Laughs ]

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.810
Fred Flintstone?
Oh, my God.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.380
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.714
I mean, why even guess?

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:29.949
-Yeah.
-Why even guess?

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:33.252
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.288
Did your phone
just like explode?
-Yes, yes.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:39.258
[ Laughter ]
Yes.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:40.259
"Scooby-Doo!"

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:43.930
[ Laughter ]
-[ Clapping ]

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.665
Oh, my gosh!

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.000
That was the funniest thing.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.167
Oh, my God.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.668
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:53.306
Well, last night, Trump held
a rally in Omaha, Nebraska,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.408
where it was
a little chilly outside.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.876 line:0%
Check out what he said.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.979 line:0%
-Is there anyplace you
would rather be

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.048 line:0%
than a Trump rally

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.684 line:0%
[ Cheering ]
on about a 10° evening, 10°?

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.319
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.653
-It was so cold in Nebraska,

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.422
Trump almost turned
into a Creamsicle.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:13.192
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.827
I don't think Trump was
prepared for the weather.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.229
When he stepped outside,
it was like --

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.464
[ As Trump ]
Why was that told
this was a hot spot?

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.132
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:21.901
Oh.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.269
Yep, everyone was freezing.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.637
Trump supporters were like,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.105
"If only there was some way
to keep our faces warm."

00:03:27.105 --> 00:03:34.847
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.881
You could tell Trump was cold.

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:36.983
At one point,
he started speaking

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.185
in front of the engines
on Air Force One.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.320
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.590
[ Reverberating ]
Make America Great Again.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.124
Whkchkch!

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:48.026
[ Reverberating ]
Build more wall!

00:03:48.026 --> 00:03:50.797
[ Laughter ]
We need more wall!

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.931
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.931 --> 00:03:55.067
Yep, Trump said it was 10°,

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.403
which is still 10 more degrees
than the scientists

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.272
in the White House
"Science Office" have.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:02.808
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.977
[ Laughter and applause ]
Take it -- Yeah.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:08.080
It's alright.
Yeah, that was a good one.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.417
You do the math
and that's not bad, yeah.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.919
Fred Flintstone.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:20.893
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.428
Did she look like
hopeful, too,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.862
like it might be
Fred Flintstone?

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:26.132
-Why did she say it with such
conviction and authority?

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.134
-Yeah, but I just want to see
what does her face look like

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.202
after she says it.
Like is it like, "Tsk, maybe?"

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:32.372
Or is it like, "I'm just going
to say Fred Flintstone,"

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.307
like her buddies
made her do it at home.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.609
Like, "You say Fred Flintstone,
I'll give you five bucks."

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.744
-No, I think her face is like,
"I killed it."

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:40.079
Like, "Pssh, what?!"

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.614
[ Laughter ]
-Can we see it again, just --

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:45.851 line:0%
-No!
-Please, Dave?

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:47.787 line:0%
-Fred Flintstone!
-No.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.188
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah, no, no.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.690
It was hopeful.
-It was hopeful.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.024
-It was hopeful.
-It was hopeful, yeah.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.459
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.761
-It was like when you roll
that bowling ball

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.630
down the alley and you know
it's headed to the gutter,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.100
but just like --
-Anh! Maybe I got one?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.134
-Yeah.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.003
-Maybe I got one?

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.072
After his speech,
Trump quickly left Nebraska

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.208
on Air Force One,
but hundreds of his supporters

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.776 line:0%
were left stranded for hours

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:14.346 line:0%
in the frigid cold because
their buses didn't show up.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:17.550
Yep, some people were actually
treated for hypothermia.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.851
That's how bad
it's getting for Trump --

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.686
even his supporters
are turning blue.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:24.590
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.626
[ Playing funk ]

00:05:27.626 --> 00:05:37.069
♪♪

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:40.406
Before visiting Nebraska,
Trump held a rally in Michigan.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.642
At one point, he addressed
the women in the crowd

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.710
